==English==

===Prepositional phrase===
{{head|en|prepositional phrase}}

# {{lb|en|informal}} Having a streak of good [[luck]] or good [[progress]] or [[success]].
#: {{ux|en|He was '''on a roll''' with the answers that day and didn't want to stop.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1983|title={{w|Break My Stride}}|album=I Don't Speak the Language|author={{w|Matthew Wilder}}; Greg Prestopino|passage=You're '''on a roll''' and now you pray it lasts}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=Jan 2 1984|author=Charles P. Alexander|title=Cheers for a Banner Year|titleurl=http://content.time.com/time/magazine/article/0,9171,921452,00.html|journal=Time|accessdate=26 Aug 2015
|passage=With unemployment falling, incomes rising, inflation at bay and shoppers crowding into stores, the economy is entering 1984 '''on a roll'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=Feb 9 2015|author=Matthew Amalfitano|title=Torino eyeing Europa League|titleurl=http://www.independent.co.uk/sport/football/european/serie-a-five-things-we-learnt-this-weekend-including-juventus-march-to-the-title-continues-10033763.html|journal=Independent|accessdate=26 Aug 2015|location=UK
|passage=After a sluggish start to the season, Torino are '''on a roll'''. The Granata began their nine-match unbeaten streak in Serie A on December 6.}}

